-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/906a88e5-06e9-4327-b0f5-000ca09b7356
-- title:
--   Differences of dense points are dense in the difference set
-- statement:
--   Let $(z_j)$ be dense in a subset $K$ of a real normed space. Then
--   $$
--   K-K\subseteq\overline{\{z_i-z_j:\ i,j\in\mathbb N\}} .
--   $$
--
--   Countably many differences suffice to approximate every difference of points of $K$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Nonexpansive/DenseDifferences.lean#L27-L41

